<!--
  <sui-tree> — engine-backed, virtualized hierarchical tree (role=tree).

  Proves the SHARED-ENGINE REUSE law: a hierarchy is the Table engine's
  expansion model turned on, NOT a parallel engine. There is no createTree().
  The controller calls createTable({ getSubRows, getRowId, columns: [],
  initialState: { expanded } }), reads the flattened depth-first, expansion-
  respecting table.rows(), and renders it WINDOWED through createVirtualizer —
  one [role=treeitem] per VISIBLE node, indented by row.depth.

  The live Table<T> arrives via prop:tree IDENTITY binding (never a serialized
  object attribute); a `nodes` JSON attribute is the SSR/declarative fallback.

  Density is the platform axis (<html data-density>) — rows read the --density-*
  channel. There is NO density/dense prop.

  Events (host.emit): sui-toggle {id, expanded}, sui-expand-change {expanded},
  sui-select {id}, sui-node-select {selected, selectedIds}, sui-node-click
  {id, depth, index}.

  NEW SURFACE (re-port from feat/next, parity-gate pass)
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  - No tone prop on this component — rule "tone is global now" doesn't apply.
  - The row + its caret are the L1 layout keyword `row` (align/justify
    attributes), not a hand-styled flex `<div>`/`<span>` — display:flex,
    align-items and gap for both now come from the keyword, not authored CSS.
    The row's cursor/radius/ink/hover-bg are sx (`sx="radius:sm cursor:pointer
    fg:foreground hover:bg:hover-bg"` / `sx="fg:muted-foreground"` on the
    caret) instead of raw `.row`/`.caret` declarations.
  - L1 controls were already framework-composed pre-gate (sui-checkbox,
    sui-icon, sui-empty-state, sui-error-state) — nothing hand-skinned.
  - Dropped a dead line from the style block: a bare (outside any selector,
    so inert in real CSS — a browser's parser discards top-level declarations
    it can't attach to a rule) list of every token this file's raw CSS
    references, each given an EMPTY value (`--font-body: ; --foreground: ;
    …`). Harmless at runtime but pure noise; every name in it is a real,
    already-registered global token, so it worked around nothing. Not in
    feat/next; removed rather than re-ported.
  - Anatomy (light DOM, class-based — part= left on per the wave sweep note):
    .tree (root, role=tree) > .viewport > .spacer > row.row (role=treeitem,
    one per visible node) > row.caret (chevron icon), span.gutter (multi-
    select checkbox), sui-icon.node-icon / slot[name=node-icon], span.label,
    span.trailing (slot[name=node-trailing]). .tree-error / .tree-empty are
    the error/empty-state branches.

  See the second comment below (unchanged from the prior pass) for why the
  remaining `.row`/`.caret`/`.gutter`/`.node-icon`/`.label`/`.trailing` chrome
  stays in the style block rather than sx: it's overwhelmingly descendant
  state (`.row[data-selected] .node-icon`, `.row:not([data-can-expand])
  .caret`, etc.) — sx and `<variants>` both only match HOST attributes, never
  a descendant's data-* state, so there is no closed-vocabulary path to any
  of it. Not a new LANG-GAP; the prior pass already identified and documented
  this residual correctly.
-->

<prop name="nodes" type="string" default="" />
<prop name="label" type="string" default="" />
<prop name="selectable" values="none|single|multi" default="none" reflect />
<prop name="expand-on-select" type="bool" default="false" reflect />
<prop name="show-guides" type="bool" default="true" reflect />
<prop name="size" values="sm|md|lg" default="md" reflect />
<prop name="loading" type="bool" default="false" reflect />
<prop name="error" type="string" default="" />

<!--
  Residual <style> — sui-tree is largely irreducible: there is no prop here
  that channels per-value styling (size/selectable don't drive CSS rules),
  so <theme> adds nothing. The row is a flex container drawn via <row>
  (display:flex + align-items + gap live on the keyword), but most of the
  chrome is raw, because most of the rules are descendant state-driven:
  they target data-* attrs that live ON the row, not host — and <variants>
  selectors only match host attrs.

  Rules:
  - :host base (display + width + font-family + density-driven font-size +
    --sui-tree-indent indirection).
  - .viewport / .spacer layout (position + width:100% + overflow-y:auto +
    max-height panel token).
  - .row layout box (position:absolute + left + width:100% + box-sizing;
    the inline-flex row's display:flex + align-items + gap are <row>;
    padding/gap go via density-* tokens in the .row descendant CSS).
  - .row:hover, .row[data-selected], .row[data-pending], .row:focus-visible
    state rules.
  - .caret flex: none + transition + the row[data-expanded] caret rotate +
    row:not([data-can-expand]) caret visibility:hidden (descendant state).
  - .gutter / .node-icon .row[data-selected] .node-icon color (descendant
    reacts to row[data-selected]).
  - .label raw `flex:1` + min-width + white-space + overflow + text-overflow.
  - .trailing margin-inline-start:auto (the `auto` margin is not in sx).
  - :host([show-guides]) .row::before pseudo-element.
  - @media (forced-colors: active) CanvasText outline.
-->
<style>
  :host {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: var(--density-text);
    color: var(--foreground);
    --sui-tree-indent: var(--density-row-px);
  }
  :host([hidden]) { display: none; }

  .viewport {
    position: relative;
    width: 100%;
    overflow-y: auto;
    max-height: var(--panel-max-h-md);
  }
  .spacer { position: relative; width: 100%; }

  .row {
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    width: 100%;
    box-sizing: border-box;
    padding: var(--density-row-py) var(--density-row-px);
    gap: var(--density-row-gap);
    outline: none;
    transition: background-color var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-out);
  }
  .row:hover { background: var(--hover-bg); }
  .row[data-selected] { background: var(--selected-bg); font-weight: var(--font-weight-medium); }
  .row[data-pending] {
    cursor: default;
    color: var(--muted-foreground);
    font-style: italic;
  }
  .row[data-pending]:hover { background: transparent; }
  .row:focus-visible { box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 var(--ring-width) var(--ring-color); }

  .caret {
    flex: none;
    width: var(--density-icon);
    height: var(--density-icon);
    color: var(--muted-foreground);
    transition: transform var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-out);
  }
  .row[data-expanded] .caret { transform: rotate(90deg); }
  .row:not([data-can-expand]) .caret { visibility: hidden; }

  .gutter { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; flex: none; }

  .node-icon {
    flex: none;
    color: var(--muted-foreground);
  }
  .row[data-selected] .node-icon { color: var(--foreground); }

  .label {
    flex: 1;
    min-width: 0;
    white-space: nowrap;
    overflow: hidden;
    text-overflow: ellipsis;
  }
  .trailing { margin-inline-start: auto; color: var(--muted-foreground); font-size: var(--text-xs); }

  :host([show-guides]) .row::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    inset-block: 0;
    inset-inline-start: calc(var(--sui-tree-indent) * 0.5);
    border-inline-start: 1px dashed var(--border);
  }

  @media (forced-colors: active) {
    .row:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid CanvasText; outline-offset: -2px; }
  }
</style>


<controller>
// <sui-tree> controller — engine-backed, virtualized hierarchical tree.
//
// REUSES the Table engine (createTable with getSubRows+expanded) and the shipped
// createVirtualizer; there is NO createTree(). The live `Table<T>` arrives via
// the `prop:tree` IDENTITY host property (never serialized); a `nodes` JSON
// attribute is the SSR/declarative fallback. The windowed body renders
// `tree.rows()` (flattened, depth-first, expansion-respecting) through a
// createVirtualizer viewport, one [role=treeitem] per VISIBLE node.
//
// Templates declare, controllers do: mutations + emit live in mount's delegated
// listeners; aria/level/posinset/setsize are derived in the TEMPLATE from the
// TreeRowView this builds.
//
// Authority: build-spec §"Controller shape", §"Backbone reuse", Slices 2-4.

import { controller, signal, derived, ref } from '@ship/sui-runtime'
import type { ViewScope } from '@ship/sui-runtime'
import { createVirtualizer, type Virtual } from '@ship/sui-runtime/virtual'
import { createTable, type Table } from '../sui-table/engine/create-table'
import type { TreeNode } from '../sui-tree-view/sui-tree-view.controller'
import { parseJsonNodes } from './decode'
import { treeTableOptions } from './sui-tree.engine'
import { windowTreeRows } from './sui-tree.view'
import { wireTreeInteractions } from './sui-tree.interactions'
import type { Scope } from './sui-tree.sui'

type AnyTreeNode = TreeNode & Record<string, unknown>

/** Fallback indent step (px) when the density channel is unmeasured (jsdom). */
const INDENT_STEP = 16
/** Row-height estimate seed for the virtualizer (density-derived at runtime). */
const ROW_HEIGHT = 32

/** A stable empty engine so the windowed read never branches on null. */
function emptyTree(): Table<AnyTreeNode> {
  return createTable<AnyTreeNode>(treeTableOptions<AnyTreeNode>({ data: [] }))
}

export default controller({
  // `nodes` (string) + `selectable` (enum) are read imperatively from the host
  // in mount/interactions — they are not part of the compiler-emitted `Scope`.
  scope: (_ctx: ViewScope<Scope>) => {
    const treeSig = signal<Table<AnyTreeNode> | null>(null)
    const viewportEl = ref<HTMLDivElement>(null)

    const EMPTY = emptyTree()
    const tree = derived<Table<AnyTreeNode>>(() => treeSig() ?? EMPTY)

    const virt: Virtual = createVirtualizer({
      count: () => tree().rows().length,
      estimateSize: (_index) => ROW_HEIGHT,
      getScrollElement: () => viewportEl(),
      overscan: 8,
      getItemKey: (i) => tree().rows()[i]?.id ?? i,
    })

    const windowItems = windowTreeRows<AnyTreeNode>(tree, virt.virtualItems, () => INDENT_STEP)
    const totalSize = virt.totalSize
    const rowCount = derived<number>(() => tree().rowCount())

    // Roving-tabindex: the active row is nav's focus, defaulting to the first
    // visible row so exactly one treeitem is focusable before any key.
    const activeRowId = derived<string | null>(() => {
      const active = tree().nav.active().rowId
      if (active != null) return active
      return tree().rows()[0]?.id ?? null
    })

    const isEmptyInitial = derived<boolean>(
      () => tree().rows().length === 0 && !tree().hasActiveFilters(),
    )
    const isEmptyFiltered = derived<boolean>(
      () => tree().rows().length === 0 && tree().hasActiveFilters(),
    )

    return {
      treeSig,
      viewportEl,
      tree,
      virt,
      windowItems,
      totalSize,
      rowCount,
      activeRowId,
      isEmptyInitial,
      isEmptyFiltered,
    }
  },

  mount(state, host) {
    // ── prop:tree IDENTITY wiring ────────────────────────────────────────────
    // The engine is a LIVE JS reference assigned to the host `tree` property
    // (never a stringified attribute). Route it into the scope signal so the
    // windowed render reacts.
    Object.defineProperty(host, 'tree', {
      configurable: true,
      get: () => state.tree,
      set: (t: Table<AnyTreeNode> | null) => {
        state.treeSig = t
      },
    })

    // SSR fallback: build an engine from the `nodes` JSON attribute when no
    // identity engine was assigned (the sui-combobox pattern).
    if (state.treeSig == null) {
      const raw = (host as { nodes?: string }).nodes ?? host.getAttribute('nodes') ?? ''
      const parsed = parseJsonNodes(raw)
      if (parsed.length > 0) {
        const selAttr = host.getAttribute('selectable') ?? 'none'
        state.treeSig = createTable<AnyTreeNode>(
          treeTableOptions<AnyTreeNode>({
            data: parsed as AnyTreeNode[],
            selectable: selAttr !== 'none',
            multiSelect: selAttr === 'multi',
          }),
        )
      }
    }

    // ── Delegated caret/row interactions + deduped engine-state emission ──────
    const stop = wireTreeInteractions(host, () => state.tree, {
      expandOnSelect: () => host.hasAttribute('expand-on-select'),
      selectable: () => (host.getAttribute('selectable') ?? 'none') !== 'none',
      multi: () => (host.getAttribute('selectable') ?? 'none') === 'multi',
      navRoleSelector: '[role="tree"]',
      getWindow: () => state.$signals.windowItems(),
    })

    return () => {
      stop()
      state.virt.dispose()
    }
  },
})

</controller>
{#if error() !== ''}
<div class="tree-error" part="error" role="alert">
  <error-state>{error()}</error-state>
</div>
{:else if isEmptyInitial()}
<div class="tree-empty" part="empty" role="status">
  <slot name="empty"><empty-state></empty-state></slot>
</div>
{:else if isEmptyFiltered()}
<div class="tree-empty" part="empty" role="status">
  <slot name="empty">
    <empty-state>
      <button slot="action" type="button" data-action="clear-filters">Clear filters</button>
    </empty-state>
  </slot>
</div>
{:else}
<div
  class="tree"
  part="tree"
  role="tree"
  aria-label={label() || null}
  aria-multiselectable={selectable() === 'multi' ? 'true' : null}
>
  <div class="viewport" part="viewport" bind:this={viewportEl}>
    <div class="spacer" part="spacer" style:height={`${totalSize()}px`}>
      {#for w of windowItems() key={w.key}}
        <row
          class="row"
          part="row"
          align="center"
          role="treeitem"
          data-node-id={w.id}
          aria-level={w.level}
          aria-posinset={w.posInSet}
          aria-setsize={w.setSize}
          aria-rowindex={w.index + 1}
          aria-expanded={w.canExpand ? (w.expanded ? 'true' : 'false') : null}
          aria-selected={selectable() !== 'none' ? (w.selected ? 'true' : 'false') : null}
          data-can-expand={w.canExpand ? 'true' : null}
          data-expanded={w.expanded ? 'true' : null}
          data-selected={w.selected ? 'true' : null}
          data-pending={w.pending ? 'true' : null}
          tabindex={w.id === activeRowId() ? '0' : '-1'}
          style:transform={`translateY(${w.start}px)`}
          style:padding-inline-start={`calc(var(--density-row-px) + ${w.indent}px)`}
          sx="radius:sm cursor:pointer fg:foreground hover:bg:hover-bg"
        >
          <row class="caret" part="caret" aria-hidden="true" align="center" justify="center"
            sx="fg:muted-foreground">
            <sui-icon name="chevron-right" size="xs"></sui-icon>
          </row>

          {#if selectable() === 'multi'}
            <span class="gutter" part="gutter">
              <input
                type="checkbox"
                size="sm"
                aria-label={`Select ${w.label}`}
                prop:checked={w.checked}
                prop:indeterminate={w.someSelected}
              />
            </span>
          {/if}
          {#if w.icon !== ''}
            <sui-icon class="node-icon" part="node-icon" name={w.icon} size="sm"></sui-icon>
          {:else}
            <slot name="node-icon"></slot>
          {/if}
          <span class="label" part="label">{w.label}</span>
          <span class="trailing"><slot name="node-trailing"></slot></span>
        </row>
      {/for}
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
{/if}
